TEST 38148 -- IPv6 QoS - Exploratory testing
===========================================================================
Run: 2026-09-22, tb470

VERDICT: UNMEASURED -- the case has no steps.

In ck.db, AWPTCM-T38148 has num_steps = 0, no precondition and no expected
result. "Exploratory testing" is a description of an activity, not a procedure,
so there is nothing to execute against or to grade PASS/FAIL. Recorded as a
case-definition gap rather than invented.

WHAT WAS EXERCISED ANYWAY, in the course of the other QoS cases, all PASS:
  - IPv6 classification by source address, via a hardware IPv6 ACL matched in
    a class-map: AWPTCM-T13819 (2001:db8:50::/64 -> dscp 46, others untouched)
  - IPv6 DSCP marking is decoded at egress from the IPv6 traffic-class field
    by the same harness used for IPv4
So IPv6 QoS is demonstrably functional on this platform even though this
particular case cannot be graded.

If exploratory IPv6 QoS coverage is wanted, the useful next targets are the
ones this bench cannot reach today: IPv6 under congestion (queueing/wrr, see
13549/13553) and IPv6 policing rates, both of which need a line-rate source.
